[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186096648,
      "id": "27d5c96d-ca13-5c1e-83d3-0dc9f6da0f83",
      "title": "Determining Whether Two Vectors are Parallel"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7af3086b-d453-5cde-8cfe-527fb842e2e0",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $\\lambda (-12\\mathbf{a} + 8\\mathbf{b})$ and $18\\mathbf{a} - 12\\mathbf{b}$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n18\\mathbf{a} - 12\\mathbf{b}=\\lambda (-12\\mathbf{a} + 8\\mathbf{b}).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}(-12\\mathbf{a} + 8\\mathbf{b})=\\lambda (-12\\mathbf{a} + 8\\mathbf{b}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(-12\\mathbf{a} + 8\\mathbf{b})$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=-12\\mathbf{a} + 8\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nSince $u$ is non-zero,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=-\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "64e909ee-7a25-5e39-8d4c-e82a75c68947",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "4846ad0a-8c96-5b4b-8609-9be79135cd64",
