    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3d8b2d65-384d-566e-8262-85e94b9edabe",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $-3\\mathbf{a} - 12\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\lambda (4\\mathbf{a} + 16\\mathbf{b})$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n-3\\mathbf{a} - 12\\mathbf{b}=\\lambda (4\\mathbf{a} + 16\\mathbf{b}).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{4}(4\\mathbf{a} + 16\\mathbf{b})=\\lambda (4\\mathbf{a} + 16\\mathbf{b}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(4\\mathbf{a} + 16\\mathbf{b})$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=4\\mathbf{a} + 16\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{4}\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nSince $u$ is non-zero,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$",
